text:
I wrote both briefs for issue #102 and the harness accepted them, so they can no longer be changed. I changed nothing in the repo.

**Builder brief** walks through building `packages/jsonl-lint`:
- its `package.json`;
- a `lint(text)` function in `src/index.js`;
- the command-line script in `bin/jsonl-lint.js`;
- `node:test` tests for the five cases the issue names;
- the tool's README and a new entry in the root README;
- one PR whose body says `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`, with the test workflow green at its head.

It also tells the builder to update `package-lock.json` with the new workspace. The issue doesn't mention this, but CI runs `npm ci`, and that fails if the lock file doesn't include the workspace.

**Verifier brief** has six checks, one per acceptance line, in the issue's order. Each says what to run at the PR head (the script against small test files, the exported `lint` function, the workspace tests, `gh pr view` / `gh pr checks`, and `npm ci && npm test`) and what counts as PASS or FAIL.

The verifier's Advisory section holds stricter tests that are not pass/fail conditions:
- the lock file includes the new workspace;
- Windows line endings (CRLF) don't cause false errors;
- the script has a shebang and is executable;
- error rows go to stdout, and the exit-code-2 cases print nothing to stdout.
